    Brightness behaviour of the ANA38401 AMSA05RB06 panel, taken from the stock
    T865XXU6DXE1 vendor framework overlay (config_screenBrightnessBacklight / Nits,
    config_autoBrightnessLevels / DisplayValuesNits, config_autoBrightnessHbmAmbientLux).
    Backlight values are the stock levels divided by the kernel maximum (355).
    Levels above 255 are the panel's high brightness mode (378 to 500 nits). As on
    stock they are only reached by automatic brightness from 3000 lux. Stock has no
    time limit for that mode; here it is limited to 10 minutes in any 30.

    Thermal limits as in the stock thermal policy (siop_gts6l_sm8150): brightness is
    capped at level 206 from an estimated skin temperature of 41 C and at level 140
    from 43 C. The thermal HAL reports these as "moderate" and "severe", see
    configs/thermal.
-->
